 identically to C**. Rather than weakening the assertion, the harness detects this mechanically and permits *only* that exact `signal(11)`↔`signal(6)` pairing. Debug assertions were left enabled on purpose, since they also prove the translation never panics where the C wraps.\n2. **Double `finalize_logger` is nondeterministic in the C itself** — the same C `.so` produced both `exited(0)` and `SIGABRT`. There is no stable behaviour to compare, so it's asserted at source level instead: neither implementation clears its static after `fclose`, so the Rust doesn't \"fix\" the bug.\n3. **The `max_tasks * sizeof(Task)` sign-extension is unobservable at runtime** — I measured that across the whole negative `int32` range, sign- and zero-extension both exceed 558 GB, so `malloc` returns `NULL` either way. Covered differentially over all boundaries *plus* pinned at source level (new row E23).\n\n**Suite is not vacuous:** I injected 19 mutants one at a time into `translation/src/` (wrong severity tag, `strncpy` off-by-one, dropped forced NUL, `>=`→`>` capacity guard, 0-based print index, pre- vs post-increment `priority`, `strchr('\\n')`→`'\\r'`, `EXIT_FAILURE` 1→2, fopen `\"a\"`→`\"w\"`, and 10 more). **All 19 were killed.**\n\nOne process note: during mutation testing `$TMPDIR` changed between tool calls, which destroyed my backup and deleted `src/`. I restored all five files verbatim from the originals (line counts and full-suite results confirm exact restoration), then re-ran everything with a repo-local backup. `c_src/` is untouched — all six files still carry their original checkout mtime."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2374,"cache_read_input_tokens":159385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2374,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26fdf2c9-8a04-4781-b0e7-60b05b0d656b",